<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Hubudagang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1115">1115</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchen-campaigns-against-the-liao-dynasty">Jurchen campaigns against the Liao dynasty</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Hubudagang was fought in 1115 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchens">Jurchen</a> leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizu-of-jin">Wanyan Aguda</a>, newly proclaimed emperor of the Jin dynasty, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao</a> emperor Tianzuo. Aguda's small army routed a far larger Liao force, a defeat that broke Liao power in the north-east and opened the way to the fall of the dynasty.</p></div>
